lib/test/ - libcgra unit tests
==============================

    test_cgra.c   assert.h unit tests driven against the sim: emulator (no
                  FPGA). Covers config-word packing, the ID handshake, the
                  configure/write/run/read primitives, every vector kernel vs.
                  a host reference, the fixed SHL-of-negative path, the dot
                  product, NULL-argument error codes, and the NACK retry path
                  with its stats counters.

Output is TAP-style ("ok N - ...", a "1..N" plan, a pass/fail summary); the
binary exits non-zero if any check fails.

Run (make -f ../lib.mk <target>)
--------------------------------
    test                 build + run (assertions forced on)
    PROFILE=asan test    same, under AddressSanitizer + UBSan
    valgrind             run the tests under valgrind (needs valgrind)

Assertions stay live even in a release build: the test binary is compiled
-UNDEBUG so assert() fires regardless of PROFILE.
